	Define $M_k = \max\left\{ [\hat\gamma_{k}]_i : i \in J_* \right\}$ for $k \in K_2$.
	When $\{ M_k \}_{k \in K_2}$ is bounded, then we can find $K_3 \subseteq K_2$ and $\gamma_* \in \R^p_+$ such that $[\gamma_*]_i = 0$ for $i \notin J_*$ and $\lim_{ K_3 \ni k \to \infty} [\hat \gamma_k]_i = [\gamma_*]_i$ for $i \in J_*$.
